        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dec1a3ce-3d43-53a6-a24b-be067fa2b8cb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Karl Kraepelin\n- Animals: Scorpions, Boiga kraepelini\n- Biology Topics: Arachnid taxonomy, animal morphology\n- Organizations: Satellite High School\n\nFacts:\n- Karl Matthias Friedrich Magnus Kraepelin was born on 14 December 1848 in Neustrelitz and died on 28 June 1915 in Hamburg.\n- Karl Kraepelin was a German naturalist who specialized in the study of scorpions, centipedes, spiders, and solfugids.\n- In 1899, Karl Kraepelin published the monograph \"Scorpiones und Pedipalpi\" in Berlin.\n- Karl Kraepelin's 1899 monograph \"Scorpiones und Pedipalpi\" was an exhaustive survey of the taxonomy of the order Scorpiones.\n- Scorpions have eight legs, a pair of grasping pedipalps, and a narrow segmented tail that is often curved forward over the back and ends with a venomous stinger.\n- The specific name \"kraepelini\" in Boiga kraepelini honors Karl Kraepelin.\n- Satellite High School has the Scorpion as its mascot.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "e7d29beb-d875-54f3-b91f-c805d8f0358c",
        "text": "Page: Karl Kraepelin. Sentence: Karl Matthias Friedrich Magnus Kraepelin (14 December 1848 Neustrelitz – 28 June 1915 Hamburg), was a German naturalist who specialised in the study of scorpions, centipedes, spiders and solfugids, and was noted for his monograph \"\"Scorpiones und Pedipalpi\"\" (Berlin) in 1899, which was an exhaustive survey of the taxonomy of the Order Scorpiones.\nPage: Scorpion. Sentence: They have eight legs and are easily recognized by the pair of grasping pedipalps and the narrow, segmented tail, often carried in a characteristic forward curve over the back, ending with a venomous stinger.\nPage: Boiga kraepelini. Sentence: Its specific name \"kraepelini\" honours Karl Kraepelin, a German naturalist.\nPage: Satellite High School. Sentence: The mascot is the Scorpion.",
